        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string>Export the current ERP5/ZODB representation of an installed Business Template\n
into the standard repository format (filesystem), then commit it to git.\n
\n
STAGED and CONFLICT-PROTECTED: the ERP5 representation is first exported to a temporary\n
directory, validated (Python syntax, XML), and compared against the current repository\n
and baseline. It refuses to overwrite unrelated local edits or drop untracked files\n
(repository_write_conflict) unless force=true. dry_run=true previews without writing.\n
\n
Filesystem writes are not part of the ZODB transaction; the repository change is\n
recorded as a single git commit after validation succeeds. The tool never leaves the\n
working repository half-exported.\n
\n
Requires development permissions (Manager) and a changelog message for the commit.\n
\n
Returns JSON with: success, operation=\'export\', business_template, dry_run,\n
zodb_to_repository, would_change, conflicts, export_to_repository_safe, revision.\n
</string> </value>
